aquamarine: optionally CPU-wait on the render fence before KMS commits

Base: aquamarine a79fb21b (v0.14.0) + omarchy-android
patches/aquamarine/0001-wayland-carry-proven-Android-KGSL-buffer-pipeline.patch
(the library shipped in /opt/omarchy-android/aquamarine on vegas).

vegas (MT6835): mali_kbase attaches no dma_resv fences to shared dma-bufs and
the vendor mediatek_v2 KMS driver never waits on a plane's IN_FENCE_FD
(mtk_fb_wait()'s dma_resv wait is commented out; mediatek-drm.ko imports no
dma_fence_wait*/drm_atomic_helper_wait_for_fences). A frame Hyprland has just
submitted to the GPU can therefore be scanned out half-rendered.

Hyprland 0.56.1 already exports an EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync fd for each
frame (endRender -> setExplicitInFence) whenever the EGL display has the
extension, but aquamarine only forwards it when the DRM device has syncobj
timelines.

AQ_KMS_CPU_FENCE_WAIT=1: before a real (non-test) commit with a buffer,
poll() the consumer's in-fence (bounded at 100 ms). Logs a summary every 600
frames ("drm: KMS CPU fence wait: ...").
AQ_KMS_FENCE_WITHOUT_TIMELINES=1: report supportsExplicit (and attach
IN_FENCE_FD) when the CRTC/plane expose OUT_FENCE_PTR/IN_FENCE_FD even without
timelines. Correct for drivers that honour IN_FENCE_FD; NOT sufficient on vegas.
Both default off, so other hardware is unaffected. Also adds <cmath>, which
GCC 16 needs for std::round in DRM.cpp.

